{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453034-wondering-about-wolf-gifts-2e","id":453034,"title":"Wondering about Wolf Gifts(2e)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-22T12:52:29-07:00","id":453034,"title":"Wondering about Wolf Gifts(2e)","content":"Hey all! I've heard a lot of people talking about the new edition, and it sounds pretty awesome. Thing is, I haven't heard much about Wolf Gifts....well, except for Father's Form. So, what do you think about them? What Gift is your favorite? What Facet? What sort of cool stuff can you do with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T13:03:39-07:00","id":453062,"title":"","content":"There are three: The Changing Gift, the Hunting Gift and the Pack Gift. Changing gifts are REALLY Thematic and their's just something cool about the idea of instinctively knowing how to skin and preserve flesh so that it might be worn. The new version of partial change is nifty too. (Sorry I'm not being more specific, I'm away from my copy) My only regret is that there are no Territory Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T13:09:04-07:00","id":453068,"title":"","content":"They've added a facet that lets you change sex, which I always felt was missing from 1e given the whole Luna thing. <br /> <br /> Also the Impossible Spoor facet lets you track someone by noticing things like disturbed photons where their shadow was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T13:27:08-07:00","id":453094,"title":"","content":"I really like the wolf gifts. I don't know what more to say than that, but on my list of things to get, they show up the most, followed by Technology Shadow Gifts. It's a nice mix of things that have a wide range of usage. And a couple of them offer permanent enhancements, namely Honed Senses and Beast Talker, which I think are great for Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Skin Thief, I've mentioned in another thread, is one of my favorites but I have an issue with its duration. Of course, the way fetishes are built it seems you could use those to get more use out of Skin Thief with relative ease.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd like clarification on is Gaze of the Moon. Essentially when you use it, you subject the target to the 'full effects of Lunacy as if the Uratha was in Gauru form,' and you can pick which Lunacy Condition you inflict them with. The issue that came up brought up points like, the target only gets a Lunacy Condition if they fail a Lunacy roll, if they succeed they get a normal succeeding breaking point Condition, Guilty, Shaken or Spooked. And if the target has a dramatic failure, which is more likely at higher levels of Primal Urge, since the Lunacy roll is the target's Wits+Resolve -2, for gauru, and other modifiers, with an increasing penalty with Primal Urge, you become more likely to inflict a Dramatic Failure. And Dramatic Failure doesn't cause any Lunacy Conditions, it causes the target to eventually become Wolf-Blooded. So in the end the benefit of the ability, being able to choose the Lunacy Condition you inflict, has an infrequent chance at occurring, and could leave you with not merely an unaffected target who's gained all their Willpower back in the case of an exceptional success, but a character who has avoided any Conditions and will eventually become a wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> Plus, essentially you're always causing a Breaking Point, does this mean you can just grind a person's integrity down to 0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-22-2015, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T13:57:54-07:00","id":453135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453034-wondering-about-wolf-gifts-2e?p=453068#post453068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've added a facet that lets you change sex, which I always felt was missing from 1e given the whole Luna thing.<br /> <br /> Also the Impossible Spoor facet lets you track someone by noticing things like disturbed photons where their shadow was.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit my first instinct was to roll my eyes BUT seeing as its an Honor facet (meaning that its more common among the Elodoth) and wolves can now breed I think it makes perfect sense and is VERY cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T14:07:35-07:00","id":453136,"title":"","content":"Wait, on a chance die you regular-fail 8 times out of ten. How is that less likely than a dramatic faliure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T14:14:06-07:00","id":453140,"title":"","content":"It isn't, but the increasing penalties are more likely to bring you to a Chance Die, which turns the chance of a Dramatic Failure from 0 to 10%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T14:33:42-07:00","id":453165,"title":"","content":"I think on a dramatic failure the becoming a wolfblooded happens <i>in addition </i>to the results of failing normally anyway. Otherwise it's not particularly dramatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T14:48:42-07:00","id":453174,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of things. But when it comes to mechanics until I homebrew I can only work off of what they give me, and it doesn't say that anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-22-2015, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T14:53:08-07:00","id":453199,"title":"","content":"The Gift of Change is roughly analogous to Mother Luna's gifts, ditto th Gift of Hunting and Father Wolf gifts. The Gift of the Pack is new (afaik, unless it had an anolgue in a supplement I didn't know about). They're all very cool and thematic, and where a lot of the Shadow Gifts have somewhat specific concepts, I feel like all of the Wolf Gifts could fit very well on just about any werewolf character. The Gift of Change is probably my favorite overall, between the Cunning Facet that lets you wear an animal or human's skin to replace your Urshul form with that animal or person's appearance, the Honor Facet that lets you change sex, and the Wisdom Facet that works like the new Partial Change. Impossible Spoor (Huntimg, Wisdom) is definitely my favorite Facet among the Wolf Gifts. I love the idea of an Iron Master tracking her prey by his smartphone's wifi footprint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T15:03:10-07:00","id":453225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453034-wondering-about-wolf-gifts-2e?p=453174#post453174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it doesn't say that anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it needs to. I mean thematically I wouldn't have them develop the tell until the end of the scene at the earliest, so in the meantime they've been hit with lunacy hard enough to alter their fundamental nature. You really think they're just gonna just shrug that off? Don't be silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T16:40:58-07:00","id":453350,"title":"","content":"The first thing I thought when I saw the gender change Facet, is &quot;YAY, Uratha trans characters can have a cheap and supereffective surgery!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 03-22-2015, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T16:44:54-07:00","id":453354,"title":"","content":"Which is useful when you consider that their regeneration might cause some issues with the standard version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T17:03:28-07:00","id":453377,"title":"","content":"I really like the Wolf Gifts. As I'm trying to put together a pack who's totem benefit includes the Pack Dynamics Merit, picking up Pack Awareness (Gift of the Pack, Wisdom) is one of my first priorities. Impossible Spoor will also be awesome to have.<br /> A lot of them, those two included to some extent, seem very much like flavor gifts more than real function gifts. Take the Skin Thief one that Charlaquin brought up for example. It would let you be a near-perfect mimic of someone, but you'd have to skin them first, spend 5 essence, and then only use it until you shapeshifted. I get the feeling the greater use of that gift is to switch out your Urhan form for something more location appropriate. A pack of wolves is suspicious most places, but that's far more true in places that don't have wolves.<br /> Now, sure, this is a Storytelling Game, and as such flavor is as important or perhaps more important. The main thing I'm getting at with these is that it seems appropriate that they take fewer Experiences to pick up than the rest of the Shadow gifts, as per the chart on the character making page. There's a discrepency between the chart and the text on a nearby page, but I like the chart's take on it. And I like the Wolf Gifts and plan to buy many of the cheap little buggers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T17:25:02-07:00","id":453420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453034-wondering-about-wolf-gifts-2e?p=453199#post453199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the idea of an Iron Master tracking her prey by his smartphone's wifi footprint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! This!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}